The censored-regression SVM quadratic program and the five-decimal support and
intercept conventions in R/svm.R follow survivalsvm 0.0.6, whose DESCRIPTION
credits Cesaire J. K. Fouodo and declares GPL. The compact factorization,
additive prefix operators, multiplicity reduction, certified Newton solver and
linear/additive kernels are implementations in survlearning. Since 0.2.1,
survivalsvm is needed only for optional independent reference tests, not for
fitting, tuning or prediction. See https://github.com/imbs-hl/survivalsvm.

The explicit dense solver calls quadprog::solve.QP through its exported API.
Its constraint order preserves the convention of the former pracma::quadprog
wrapper (pracma, Hans W. Borchers, GPL >= 3); pracma is no longer a dependency.

All other optional engine packages are called through their exported APIs.
Their authors retain authorship and their respective licenses. They are not
redistributed as embedded package sources or binaries. This wrapper does not
claim authorship of the statistical methods implemented by these engines.

R, its recommended packages and withr retain their own authorship and licenses.
